module gunbc.serving.serving_warm_admission

import std.types { NonEmptyStr, List }
import extdeps.external_authority { CitedFigureStanding }

// THE SHARED VOCABULARY BETWEEN A DEPLOYMENT ADAPTER AND THE ONE WARM STORE.
//
// The store (gunbc.serving.serving_capacity_anchor) must not hardcode one realization's refusal vocabulary -- that is
// the "one store, many rungs" rule -- and the adapter (gunbc.serving.strata_parked_tier) must not own a type the
// generic store consumes. So this tiny module owns the three generic arms the store accepts about a rung it can
// realize but may refuse, and BOTH sides import it (no cycle: anchor and strata both depend on this, neither on each
// other for this type). The adapter maps its own rich refusal into these arms; the ladder only ever sees these.
//
// The two genuinely-UNMEASURED cases fold to WarmRungUnread (a rung the store has not measured -- it contributes
// nothing and carries a read obligation), while every HARD refusal folds to WarmRungRefused (the store cannot be
// used here at all -- it contributes nothing and the held bound NAMES why, so a refusal never masquerades as a
// missing reading). Keeping them distinct is the whole point: an unread rung owes a measurement; a refused rung owes
// none and must not be handed one (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed; review 92430 / gentle-swift-129).
// WarmAdmit carries the standings of the deployment facts its admission rested on (gentle-swift-129, review 92497):
// an ASSUMED restore contract is a bet that must reach the tally as a TranscribedUncited obligation, so the ladder
// shows a rung that admitted on an unverified contract rather than consuming it as fact. An ESTABLISHED contract is a
// fact and adds no standing. Empty means admitted on established evidence alone. This is the SAME CitedFigureStanding
// the cache/budget readings use; it is deliberately NOT List<NonEmptyStr> so cited evidence and uncited bets share one
// carrier if a future adapter cites one.
type ServingWarmAdmission
  = WarmAdmit { admission_standings: List<CitedFigureStanding> }
  | WarmRungUnread { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | WarmRungRefused { reason: NonEmptyStr, cites: NonEmptyStr }
